{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/754907-challenge-mound","id":754907,"title":"Challenge mound?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-04T14:17:08-08:00","id":754907,"title":"Challenge mound?","content":"So, here's one thing that has made me and few of my friends wonder;<br /> <br /> Is the challenge mound, the place where garou go to challenge one another, actually from the books? Or is it a player created thing?<br /> <br /> Book and page references would be much appericated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-04T14:50:50-08:00","id":754981,"title":"","content":"First time I've heard of it, I'll try and look around a bit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T02:56:17-08:00","id":756103,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"http://asylums.insanejournal.com/emptyquarter/4442.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://asylums.insanejournal.com/emptyquarter/4442.html</a> mentions it, but that's all google found. I used DriveThruRPG's in book search beta on my extensive library but came up empty.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T03:26:40-08:00","id":756160,"title":"","content":"Text search for DTR books won't help for older books as they are not OCRed. They are image scans rather then text and pictures in layout.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T03:59:29-08:00","id":756209,"title":"","content":"Older books are also OCRed on drivethru (unlike pirated downloads from the internet). The text usually is behind the scanned images (as opposed to PDFs generated directly from source documents). The OCR-text is often flawed, with some characters wrong, faulty spaces and strange line breaks, but I got matches in those books, too. But sure, it could be that some older books weren't properly searched.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:21:46-08:00","id":756237,"title":"","content":"Really? That actually increases my interest in DTR stuff as I thought I'd be unable to search all of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8760-cogliostro","name":"Cogliostro","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8760_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T04:45:42-08:00","id":756256,"title":"","content":"Sure.<br /> I just tried to copy a paragraph from Litany of the tribes and every word was in its own line, but the text was correct. And after a quick &quot;replace all&quot; in a text editor I hade the text:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Of course, the other Garou rose up in rage. The Silver Fangs called in the tribes once again. They wished us to be punished. The Get of Fenris asked for the right to slay us. The Shadow Lords requested that we disband, for we had grown too large. The Children of Gaia, Black Furies and Stargazers voiced their opposition to the Impergium. The Bone Gnawers agreed, but would not come forward. As the days of the Grand Moot grew to a close, the Silver Fangs ordered the destruction of the second city. </div> </div> </div>Especially when discussing rules over the internet is is pretty nice to be able to quote the rules easily...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:28:44-08:00","id":756672,"title":"","content":"I haven't found anything about it, and likewise I don't remember it ever being a thing.<br /> <br /> It's possible it's from the novels instead of the gaming supplements. But you'd think terminology like this would evident in a few key books (aka those discussing Sept positions in detail, and Sept structures).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T09:45:32-08:00","id":756692,"title":"","content":"As far as I know, it most likely started as a LARP thing, and then was assumed canon and taken into online games from there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T11:54:52-08:00","id":757042,"title":"","content":"Or people just liked the idea and used it themselves rather than assume anything. I've never seen anyone say it's canon, but I have seen it be a thing in many places under many guises over the years. I think it's just a place to organise posts online or create a continuous and consistent place for all to know and understand the expectations in play. As long as rules are given prior of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-05T16:31:32-08:00","id":757451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Somuchlove</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/754907-challenge-mound?p=757042#post757042\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or people just liked the idea and used it themselves rather than assume anything. I've never seen anyone say it's canon, but I have seen it be a thing in many places under many guises over the years. I think it's just a place to organise posts online or create a continuous and consistent place for all to know and understand the expectations in play. As long as rules are given prior of course.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've got no problem with the whole concept or it being there. This is simply to figure out what is house rule and what is canon, since there has been confusion about similar things in games.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-06T06:35:05-08:00","id":758536,"title":"","content":"'Guardians of the Caerns' has some info on CAerns and Septs. Mostnotably for this discussion would be the Assembl area found on Pages 22-23<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assembly Area: The assembly area is the social heart of the sept. It is the place where most moots are held, where challenges are met, and where counsels are kept. The layout of such a place varies considerably, but it must be large enough to accommodate all sept members. The assembly area ideally has room for visiting Garou as well, although in truly cramped caems, some septs get around the space problem by conducting their moots in the Umbra. </div> </div> </div>Septs have a social area where challenges are met. The layout and setting can vary. Ideally a place big enough for even visitors to attend.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As with the rest of the caem, this section reflects the caem type, totem and sept. A sept with an air- aspected totem such as Eagle or Wind is usually very open to the elements, while one dedicated to Owl or a spirit of the deep forest may be surrounded by high trees that block the sky. Many gathering areas have special places set aside for the sept leader or the elders; this may be a throne, a boulder, or even a raised platform of earth. </div> </div> </div>Reflects to the nature of the Caern. Gives some examples.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A central focal point, such as a tree or fire ring, is common (and appeals to werewolves\u2019 sense of drama). </div> </div> </div>Can have a central focal point, a Mound could also be this and appeal to the drama.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It\u2019s considered traditional and appropriate to con- duct challenges in the assembly area, where all can witness the contest. Most duelists insist on the privielege anyway; any grudge that requires a challenge is important enough that the entire sept should witness justice being done. </div> </div> </div>It is considered tradional and appropriate. I would say that makes it canon. I woould think what it is called, how it looks like and where its found specifiically is upto the the ST determine upon reflection of the setting and story.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assembly areas are usually easily identifiable as such, simply by the physical necessity of a largish area with good line-of-sight to the center. Ancient stone circles, groves, open fields or craters are common meeting places. </div> </div> </div>Easily identifiable, Physical necessity, more examples of what the Assembly and challenge area could be like.<br /> <br /> From this I would say having a focal point for challenges that the Master of Challenge would oversee, that is available for all of the Sept to witness and gather around is canon. The term 'Challenge Mound' isnt. But if they have a mound at the Sept where challenges are held I could see it being called that by the locals.<br /> <br /> Hope that helps.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7706-somuchlove","name":"Somuchlove","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7706_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"187"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}